All 15 tests pass. Here's what I fixed across the three modules:

**`src/auth.py`** (3 bugs):
- `has_permission`: compared `required in user_roles` case-sensitively → now does `.lower()` on both sides
- `is_admin_or_owner`: used `and` instead of `or` — required both admin AND owner simultaneously

**`src/inventory.py`** (4 bugs):
- `__init__`: mutable `dict` default arg caused shared state across instances → switched to `None` with a fresh copy
- `add`: `self._stock[sku] = qty` overwrote instead of accumulating → now adds to existing stock
- `reserve`: boundary check `if qty >= self.available(sku)` rejected reserving the full available quantity (`>` instead of `>=`)
- `release`: allowed reserved count to go negative with no guard → now raises `ValueError`

**`src/text_utils.py`** (3 bugs):
- `slugify`: didn't lowercase characters → now appends `char.lower()`
- `slugify`: `replace("--","-")` only collapsed double dashes, not triple+ → replaced with `re.sub(r"-+", "-")`
- `truncate`: `text[:max_len] + suffix` counted the suffix as extra beyond `max_len` → now does `text[:max_len - len(suffix)] + suffix`
